☠ MORTAL FRETS — The Fretboard Slayer
A retro arcade-style guitar fretboard training game inspired by Mortal Kombat. Train your fretboard knowledge across 8 game modes — 4 Identification and 4 Construction — and compete on a global leaderboard.
🎮 Play Now

Game Modes
All modes play as rounds of 10 questions. Score = total errors (fewer is better). Tiebreaker: fastest time.
Identification — press the correct button
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote IDA dot on the fretboard (frets 0–12, all strings)Press the correct note nameInterval IDR (root, red) + interval dot within ±3 frets / ±2 stringsPress the correct interval (m2 → P8)Chord IDChord voicing within ±2 frets / ±2 strings of root, one note per stringPress the correct chord typeScale IDFull scale pattern in a 5-fret box, R = rootPress the correct scale name
Construction — build it on the fretboard, then press SUBMIT
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote ConstructionTarget note button illuminatedPlace ALL occurrences of that note on the fretboardInterval ConstructionR pre-placed (red), target interval illuminatedPlace the interval note anywhere at the correct pitchChord ConstructionOne chord tone pre-placed (amber), chord type illuminatedPlace remaining notes to complete the chordScale ConstructionR pre-placed in a 5-fret box, scale type illuminatedFill all scale note positions in the box

Rules

Wrong answer (ID) → stay on the same question, retry. Timer keeps running.
Wrong SUBMIT (Construction) → wrong dots turn red, missing positions turn orange. Click red to remove, click orange to confirm. Retry with SUBMIT.
Mercy ☠ → activates after 2 wrong answers/SUBMITs on the same question. Hold to reveal the full solution; release to hide. Resets each new question.
Variety → every type (note/interval/chord/scale) appears at most twice per round; the exact same question never repeats. All types are cycled before any repeats.
Box selection → Chord and Scale modes (both ID and Construction) let you work on a fixed 5-fret box or 💀 KHAOS for a random box each question.
Notation → toggle A-B-C or Do-Re-Mi at any time.


