Deploy on GitHub Pages

Upload mortal_frets.html renamed as index.html to a public repo
Go to Settings → Pages → Source: Deploy from branch → main → / (root)
Live at https://yourusername.github.io/repo-name/ within 1–2 minutes


Global Leaderboard (Firebase)
By default scores save to localStorage (local, per-browser). To enable a real global leaderboard, set up a Firebase Realtime Database and replace the FB_CONFIG block near the top of the <script> tag with your project credentials.
Separate leaderboard per mode. Sorted by errors asc → time asc.

Tech Stack
Pure HTML / CSS / JavaScript — no framework, no build step · Web Audio API (triangle oscillator + ADSR) · SVG fretboard rendered in-browser · Firebase Realtime Database (optional) · Press Start 2P + Rajdhani via Google Fonts · Retro CRT scanline effect · MK-style screen flash + shake on errors

Music Theory Coverage
Notes: all 12 chromatic, frets 0–12, all 6 strings (standard tuning E A D G B e)
Intervals: m2 · M2 · m3 · M3 · P4 · TT · P5 · m6 · M6 · m7 · M7 · P8
Chords: Maj · min · Aug · Dim · Maj7 · Dom7 · min7 · ø7 (half-dim) · °7 (dim7)
Scales: Major · Natural Minor · Harmonic Minor · Melodic Minor · Whole-Half Diminished · Half-Whole Diminished

